[method]
The paper used a large-scale GWAS and multi-trait polygenic prediction framework for cognitive and educational traits. It performed GWAS for educational attainment and for cognitive performance, math ability, and highest math; used conditional and joint multiple-SNP analysis to identify independent associated SNPs; used a Bayesian winner's-curse-adjusted framework for posterior effect-size distributions; and used MTAG to combine the GWAS summary statistics into a multi-trait score for polygenic prediction. SNP data were QC filtered by removing SNPs with strand issues, invalid or out-of-range association values, minor allele count below 25, poor imputation accuracy, indels or non-autosomal locations, invalid or duplicated coordinates, or allele mismatches; UK Biobank full-release analyses retained only SNPs in the Haplotype Reference Consortium panel. This relates to the proposed method because the proposed Elastic Net genetic proxy will be built from three PGS definitions derived from large-scale cognitive GWAS, and the paper provides a comparable source and validation context for such PGS inputs, including SNP QC and ancestry-aware polygenic prediction.
[results]
The primary educational-attainment GWAS identified 12,887 independent SNPs at P < 5e-8. A polygenic score based on these SNPs explained 11.4% of the variance in educational attainment in a UK Biobank prediction sample and 13.6% in a 23andMe prediction sample. MTAG combining educational attainment, cognitive performance, math ability, and highest math increased the number of independent SNPs to 14,251 and improved polygenic prediction to 13.6% of variance in the UK Biobank sample and 15.4% in the 23andMe sample. The supplied excerpt does not report additional quantitative outcomes for the cognitive-specific PGS definitions.
[context]
The GWAS used 280,865 adults for educational attainment and UK Biobank samples of about 11,539 for cognitive performance, math ability, and highest math. Prediction samples were independent UK Biobank and 23andMe cohorts, approximately 45,000 and 25,000 individuals, respectively. SNP QC required autosomal SNPs, minor allele count at least 25, acceptable imputation, valid strand/coordinates/alleles, and HRC panel membership for UK Biobank full-release analyses. The paper does not specify Elastic Net hyperparameters, PGS threshold selection, or genetic principal component counts; those are introduced by the proposed method.
